.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1044 AM PDT Thu Oct 29 2026

High clouds continue to stream overhead with ceilings between
15kft and 25kft and will likely lower to around 10kft late this
evening and into Friday morning. Onshore winds will increase once
again by late morning and especially so by this afternoon and into
the early evening. Winds diminish overnight and into Friday
morning. Onshore winds increase once again by Friday afternoon.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR through the TAF period. Onshore winds
increase by early afternoon and persist through the late evening
before diminishing and become light/variable Friday morning. There
is less than a 20% probability for MVFR ceilings to develop
across the Bay Area terminals early Friday morning.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR through the TAF period. Onshore
winds return later this morning and prevail through sunset this
evening. KSNS is currently experiencing (southeasterly) drainage
winds that are forecast to return onshore by early afternoon.
There is a 15-30% probability for MVFR ceilings to develop late
this evening and into Friday morning, yet the lack of a marine
layer and high cloud cover is forecast to limit this potential.

